From 2ccb587d0681fbc73bea361918c33f3d2ebbf81d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jonas=20=C3=85dahl?= <jadahl@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 10:29:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/20] demo: Don't set window state too early

The new window state is compared to the new one later, and then updated
after that. Since we updated it too early, the following check never
succeeded leading to the active state not being drawn unless something
else also triggered a redraw.
---
 demo/demo.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/demo/demo.c b/demo/demo.c
index 857f704..66216ac 100644
--- a/demo/demo.c
+++ b/demo/demo.c
@@ -1126,8 +1126,6 @@ handle_configure(struct libdecor_frame *frame,
 						     &window_state))
 		window_state = LIBDECOR_WINDOW_STATE_NONE;
 
-	window->window_state = window_state;
-
 	if (!libdecor_configuration_get_content_size(configuration, frame,
 						     &width, &height)) {
 		width = window->content_width;
-- 
